{
  // The one-shot script directory's typecheck (issue #1118, the script-directory
  // sibling of `tsconfig.test.json`'s UT-G1 job).
  //
  // `tsconfig.json` is the BUILD config — `rootDir: "src"`, `composite`, emits to
  // `dist` — so it can never include `scripts/**`: a composite project cannot see
  // files outside its `rootDir`, and anything it did see would land in the
  // deployed bundle's tree. Until this config existed, `scripts/` was outside
  // every program in the repo and NO compiler had ever read it. Nine `.ts` files
  // live there, six of which write to production Firestore; `pnpm lint` sees the
  // directory and structurally cannot see a type error in it.
  //
  // Wired into the root `typecheck` script, beside `probes/tsconfig.json` and
  // `tsconfig.test.json` — which is the half that matters: a config that merely
  // exists is run by nothing.
  //
  // `types: ["node"]` for the same reason `probes/tsconfig.json` states it
  // (#1171/#1172): these scripts use `process`, `console` and `node:*`, and
  // leaving those to automatic @types discovery made them a hoisting accident.
  //
  // `allowJs` exists for exactly one file: `prune-instance-named-kitchen-tools.ts`
  // imports `scripts/kitchen-tool-vocabulary.mjs`, which has no declarations. TS
  // reads it and INFERS its exports, so the `TOOLS as readonly SeedTool[]` at that
  // call site becomes a checked assertion instead of an assertion on `any`.
  // `checkJs` stays off: this enrols the `.mjs` as a resolvable module, not every
  // `.mjs` in the directory into a strict program.
  //
  // No `references`: like `probes/`, this recompiles the `../src/…` files two
  // scripts import inline, and stays a separate `noEmit` invocation so it cannot
  // disturb `tsc --build`'s incremental state.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
    "types": ["node"],
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false
  },
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.ts"]
}
